        "department": null,
        "description": "This course is a sequel to IML (MTH 300) and will begin with relational structures as interpretations for first-order languages. We will discuss the relationship between, on one hand mathematical theories, described in formal languages, and on the other, mathematical structures realizing those theories. This will be followed by detailed discussions on G\u00f6del\u2019s completeness theorems and its corollaries thus entering into what is known as Model Theory. We will discuss the L\u00f6wenheim-Skolem theorems, categoricity, model completeness, decidability, quantifier elimination.",
        "prerequisites_mandatory": [
            "Introduction to Mathematical Logic (MTH 300) or equivalent",
            "Abstract Algebra I (MTH 212) or equivalent"
        ],
        "prerequisites_desirable": [
            "Some exposure to universal algebra might be beneficial, but not necessary."
        ],
        "prerequisites_mandatory_resolved": [
